From dbcb922e2b94fe8b9e718f76afb04e97d7781b5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:20:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/44] fix(harbor_agent): OpenCode install on images with an
 old python3; setup failures are infra

In a 10-step OpenCode run on verified Harbor tasks, 72 of 640 trials (9 whole
prompt groups) failed in agent setup:

- 64 with "SyntaxError" on `while chunk := response.read(...)`: the binary
  installer's Python downloader used an assignment expression (Python >= 3.8)
  and f-strings (>= 3.6); the task images (R2E-Gym, SWE-Lego) have an older
  python3.
- 8 in an image with neither python3 nor curl.

The downloader is now plain Python 3 (no walrus, no f-strings). The script
tries python3, curl and wget in that order and falls back to the next tool
when a download fails (an old python3 may also lack TLS support); curl and wget
downloads are checked with sha256sum. Without any of the three it says so.

"Agent setup failed" (raised by install_from_template, and by Harbor's own
installed agents) is now classified as infra: the task image cannot run the
agent, the policy has no part in it. These rollouts were masked before as
well (no model calls, so no capture), but counted as "other".

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
